# Phase 1: Project Setup Walkthrough

> [!NOTE]
> This phase focused entirely on foundational setup, folder structuring, and backend API initialization. As a result, there is no UI to demonstrate visually yet. Starting from Phase 3 (Authentication + Users), this walkthrough will feature browser screenshots and video recordings.

## Project Structure Overview

I initialized the workspace following the "Monolith" separation requirement:
```
OrbitalX/
├── frontend/ (Vite + React + TailwindCSS)
└── backend/  (Node.js + Express + Mongoose)
```

## Work Completed

### 1. Frontend Setup
- **Framework Initialization:** Created a pure JavaScript React project via Vite.
- **Styling Configuration:** Installed `tailwindcss`, `postcss`, and `autoprefixer`.
- **Theming:** Defined the "Dark Cosmic Mission Control" theme inside [`tailwind.config.js`](file:///c:/Users/RH364/OneDrive/Desktop/orbital%20desktop/OrbitalX/frontend/tailwind.config.js).
- **Environment Setup:** Configured [`frontend/.env.local`](file:///c:/Users/RH364/OneDrive/Desktop/orbital%20desktop/OrbitalX/frontend/.env.local) to point to the backend's `http://localhost:5000`.

### 2. Backend Setup
- **Server Scaffold:** Built the foundational Express server in [`backend/server.js`](file:///c:/Users/RH364/OneDrive/Desktop/orbital%20desktop/OrbitalX/backend/server.js) with CORS, Helmet, and Morgan.
- **Dependencies:** Installed Mongoose, `dotenv`, and required security middleware.
- **Health Check API:** Created an initial `/api/health` endpoint to verify the server is running correctly.

### 3. Server Verification
Both development servers were verified to run without errors via package scripts:
- Frontend: `npm run dev`
- Backend: `npm run dev`

> [!TIP]
> The groundwork is fully prepared for Phase 2, where we will start defining Mongoose models for our database. Visual testing and `browser_subagent` captures will begin as soon as we start developing UI elements!
